course: french
lesson: 40
title: Olympiad: mixed brain-teasers ★★★
level: primary-4
stars: 3
explain: This last lesson mixes everything from the whole course - sounds, spelling, numbers, days, time, agreement and the French-speaking world - into puzzles where one sharp idea cracks each one.
explain: Some puzzles play with sound: "Un ver vert va vers un verre vert" says "vair" five times but uses four different words, and only the spelling tells them apart.
explain: Some play with history: the little hat on forêt, hôpital and île often marks an s that dropped out long ago - put it back and you get forest, hospital and isle.
explain: Picture a puzzle card in a French club: "Aujourd'hui, c'est mardi. Quel jour sera-t-il dans dix jours ?" - the trick is to jump a whole week first (mardi again) and then count three more.
explain: If you can solve these, you have travelled the whole course: you can hear French, read it, count in it and spot its traps - bravo, et à bientôt !
fact: "Un ver vert va vers un verre vert" means "A green worm goes towards a green glass"; it uses four different words that sound like "vair": ver (worm), vert (green), vers (towards) and verre (glass).
fact: The accent circonflexe often marks a lost s: forêt (forest), hôpital (hospital), fête (feast), île (isle), bête (beast), côte (coast).
fact: The letters of CHIEN can be rearranged into NICHE, and une niche is a dog's kennel.
fact: Ten days after mardi (Tuesday) is vendredi (Friday): seven days bring you back to mardi, then three more.
fact: Onze heures moins le quart is 10:45; a film of une heure et demie that starts then ends at midi et quart, 12:15.
fact: In "Les petits chats sont gris" there are 7 written but silent final consonants: les (s), petits (t, s), chats (t, s), sont (t), gris (s).
fact: A silent s or x is said as z only before a vowel sound: "Nous avons six oranges" has 2 z sounds, nous_avons and six_oranges.
fact: In "Les ___ sont vertes", vertes is feminine plural, so only a feminine plural noun fits: les pommes.
fact: Numbering the alphabet (A = 1, B = 2...), trois, huit, un, vingt spells C, H, A, T: CHAT, a cat.
fact: Swapping the colours in un chat noir and une souris blanche gives un chat blanc and une souris noire: each colour changes to match its noun.
fact: Local words: septante (70) is Belgian and Swiss, chocolatine (a chocolate pastry) is from south-west France, tuque (woolly hat) is from Quebec, and "On dit quoi ?" (what's up?) is from Côte d'Ivoire.
exercise: In "Un ver vert va vers un verre vert", how many different words sound like "vair"? | 4 | 5 | 1 | 3
exercise: What does "Un ver vert va vers un verre vert" mean? | A green worm goes towards a green glass | A green glass goes to a worm | A green worm drinks from a green glass | A worm goes green near a glass
exercise: What is a verre? | A glass | A worm | Green | Near
exercise: Put an s in place of the hat: what is forêt in English? | forest | forty | fortune | four
exercise: Which English word hides in côte? | coast | coat | cottage | cute
exercise: Which English word hides in bête? | beast | better | beat | best
exercise: Rearrange CHIEN to make the French word for a dog's kennel. | NICHE | CHINE | ECHIN | NICHÉ
exercise: Aujourd'hui, c'est mardi. Quel jour sera-t-il dans dix jours ? | vendredi | jeudi | samedi | lundi
exercise: What time is onze heures moins le quart? | 10:45 | 11:15 | 11:45 | 10:15
exercise: A film starts at onze heures moins le quart and lasts une heure et demie. When does it end? | midi et quart, 12:15 | midi moins le quart, 11:45 | une heure moins le quart, 12:45 | midi et demi, 12:30
exercise: "Les petits chats sont gris." How many final consonants are written but not said? | 7 | 5 | 6 | 4
exercise: "Nous avons six oranges." How many z sounds do you hear? | 2 | 0 | 1 | 3
exercise: "Les ___ sont vertes." Which word fits? | pommes | chapeaux | chats | pantalon
exercise: A = 1, B = 2... Decode trois, huit, un, vingt. | CHAT | CHAR | CIAT | BHAT
exercise: Un chat noir, une souris blanche. Now say a white cat and a black mouse. | un chat blanc, une souris noire | un chat blanche, une souris noir | un chat blanc, une souris noir | un chat blanche, une souris noire
exercise: Where would you hear septante? | In Belgium | In Quebec | In Paris | In Haiti
exercise: Where would you hear "On dit quoi ?" for "What's up?" | In Côte d'Ivoire | In Belgium | In Quebec | In the French Alps
test: ★★★ Ella from Dundee says, "It's all the same word, ken? Vair, vair, vair." What does the spelling show? | Four words: ver, vert, vers, verre | One word said five times for fun | Two words: vert and verre | Five words, one per vair
test: ★★★ Mason from Boston says, "Wicked, a secret code!" Which list decodes forêt, hôpital, fête, île correctly? | forest, hospital, feast, isle | fort, hotel, fat, ill, all short | forest, hotel, feast, isle | forty, hospital, fete, eel
test: ★★★ Lily from Brighton goes, "Bare hard, innit," trying to turn CHIEN into a dog's home. Why does NICHE work? | It uses the same five letters | It adds a letter | It drops the H | It's CHIEN read backwards
test: ★★★ Jake from Bradford counts on his fingers from mardi, calling mardi "one", and ends on jeudi. What's the fix? | Start from mercredi: vendredi | He's right, it's jeudi | Count 11 days, so it's samedi | Count back, so it's samedi
test: ★★★ Chloe from Toronto reads onze heures moins le quart as 11:15 and says the film ends at 12:45. What's the right ending time? | 12:15 | 12:45 | 1:15 | 11:45
test: ★★★ Oscar from Birmingham guesses "loads, mate" for silent final letters in "Les petits chats sont gris", then counts 5. Which words did he miss a second letter in? | petits and chats | les and gris, each with two | sont and gris, each with two | Only gris, with s and i
test: ★★★ Aoife from Galway says, "Sure there's no z in Nous avons six oranges at all." How many are there, and where? | Two: avons and oranges | None at all, she's right | One: only six_oranges | Three: nous, avons and six
test: ★★★ Archie from Sheffield goes, "Ey up, they could all be green, so any word fits Les ___ sont vertes." Why only pommes? | Vertes needs a feminine plural | Only apples are green | Pommes is the shortest word | Pommes is the only plural
test: ★★★ Freya from Bristol decodes trois, huit, un, vingt with A = 0 and gets "DIBU". What went wrong? | A is 1, not 0: CHAT | She mixed up huit and onze | She should count from Z backwards | Nothing, DIBU is a French word
test: ★★★ Riley from Phoenix swaps the colours and writes "un chat blanche, une souris noir". What's wrong? | Each colour must match: blanc, noire | Nothing, the colours copy straight across | Only chat is wrong: it should be une chat | Only souris is wrong: it should be un souris
test: ★★★ Kai from Auckland matches chocolatine to Quebec and tuque to France. What's right? | Chocolatine: France; tuque: Quebec | Chocolatine: Paris; tuque: Haiti | Both are from Quebec | Both are made-up words
exam: Determine the number of distinct words, homophonous with "vair", contained in the sentence "Un ver vert va vers un verre vert". | Four | Five | One | Three
exam: It is given that the present day is mardi. Ascertain the day of the week which shall fall ten days hence. | vendredi | jeudi | samedi | mercredi
exam: A film commencing at onze heures moins le quart is of one and a half hours' duration. State the hour of its conclusion. | midi et quart | midi moins le quart | une heure et quart | midi et demi
exam: Select the noun which alone satisfies the requirements of agreement in the sentence "Les ___ sont vertes". | pommes | chapeaux | chats | pantalon
